# Deploy target — Scaleway Docker host

Provisions the VM `deploy/compose.yaml` runs on: one Docker instance
plus a security group for SSH and the service port. State is remote
in an Object Storage bucket (binding spec §5); one state per
environment via workspaces. Credentials ride the environment, never
a file:

```sh
export SCW_ACCESS_KEY=…            # API key, read by both configs
export SCW_SECRET_KEY=…
export SCW_DEFAULT_PROJECT_ID=…
export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID="$SCW_ACCESS_KEY"      # the same key, for
export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="$SCW_SECRET_KEY"  # the S3 state backend
```

## Once per project

```sh
./bootstrap.sh    # provisions the state bucket, then `tofu init`
```

The bootstrap config keeps local state on purpose — the bucket is the
one resource that cannot live inside the remote state it hosts.
Commit `bootstrap/terraform.tfstate`; it contains no secrets.

## Per environment

```sh
tofu workspace new dev    # once per environment; `tofu workspace select` thereafter
tofu apply
```

SSH access uses the SSH keys uploaded to the Scaleway project, which
the instance picks up on first boot.

## Deploying

The release pipeline pushes the image; the descriptor runs it here.
Config rides the environment of this one command — nothing is baked
into the host:

```sh
DOCKER_HOST="ssh://root@$(tofu output -raw ipv4)" \
  IMAGE=<registry>/<%= projectName %>:v1.2.3 \
  docker compose -f ../../deploy/compose.yaml up -d
```
